GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP nine Interim Orders of 2020 the Interim Order applies despite the other provision` IS
    IF     `the order is one of the Interim Orders SOR/2020-88, SOR/2020-89, SOR/2020-95, SOR/2020-141, SOR/2020-169, SOR/2020-173, SOR/2020-187, SOR/2020-188 and SOR/2020-208`
       AND `the other provision is a provision of the Employment Insurance Act or of any of its regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `2021, c. 23, ss. 331 to 336 - earlier text that continues to apply from September 2021`

-- s. 331 ("Words and expressions used in sections 332 to 336 have the same meaning as in the Employment Insurance
-- Act") is `inert`, as 2018, c. 12, s. 292(1) is: it points at the Act's definitions, which the core encodes.
-- Three days divide benefit periods into four bands: September 27, 2020 (s. 333), September 26, 2021 (ss. 332, 334,
-- 335) and September 25, 2022 (ss. 335, 411). One rule places a benefit period's first day in its band and every
-- section below reads the band. The band is a question of the day the benefit period BEGINS.
-- src:3928 | 332 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as they read immediately before September 26, 2021, continue to apply in respect of an insured person or a claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins before that day:
-- src:3947 | 333 Part VIII.5 of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before September 26, 2021, continues to apply in respect of an insured person or claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 27, 2020 and ending on September 25, 2021.
-- src:3951 | 334 (1) The operation of Part VIII.1 of the Employment Insurance Act and any regulations made under that Part is suspended during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022.
-- src:3957 | 335 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as they read immediately before September 25, 2022, continue to apply in respect of an insured person or a claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022:
-- src:3984 | 411 Schedule V to the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before September 25, 2022, continues to apply in respect of a claimant whose benefit period, as those terms are defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, begins before September 25, 2022.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2021, c. 23, s. 333 (src:3947)
`Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 333 September 27, 2020` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 9 27

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provisions of 2021, c. 23, ss. 332, 334 and 335 (src:3928) (src:3951) (src:3957)
`Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 332 September 26, 2021` MEANS YearMonthDay 2021 9 26

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provisions of 2021, c. 23, s. 335 and 2022, c. 10, s. 411 (src:3957) (src:3984)
`Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 335 September 25, 2022` MEANS YearMonthDay 2022 9 25

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provisions of 2021, c. 23, ss. 332 to 335 and 2022, c. 10, s. 411 (src:3928) (src:3947) (src:3951) (src:3957) (src:3984)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
GIVETH A `ei7 Band of the day a benefit period begins`
DECIDE `Act RP 2021 c. 23 ss. 332 to 335 and 2022 c. 10 s. 411 the band of the day a benefit period begins` IS
    BRANCH IF `the first day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 333 September 27, 2020` THEN `ei7 begins before September 27, 2020`
           IF `the first day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 332 September 26, 2021` THEN `ei7 begins from September 27, 2020 to September 25, 2021`
           IF `the first day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 335 September 25, 2022` THEN `ei7 begins from September 26, 2021 to September 24, 2022`
           OTHERWISE `ei7 begins on or after September 25, 2022`

-- s. 332: the listed provisions as they read immediately before September 26, 2021 continue to apply to an insured
-- person or claimant whose benefit period begins before that day.
-- src:3926 | — 2021, c. 23, s. 332
-- src:3927 | Continued application — before September 26, 2021
-- src:3928 | 332 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as they read immediately before September 26, 2021, continue to apply in respect of an insured person or a claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins before that day:
-- src:3929 | (a) the definitions major attachment claimant and minor attachment claimant in subsection 6(1);
-- src:3930 | (b) subsection 7(2);
-- src:3931 | (c) subsection 7.1(1);
-- src:3932 | (d) subsection 12(8);
-- src:3933 | (e) subsection 21(1);
-- src:3934 | (f) subsections 22(1), (2) and (5);
-- src:3935 | (g) subsections 23(1), (1.3), (4), (4.1), (5) and (6);
-- src:3936 | (h) subsection 23.1(2);
-- src:3937 | (i) subsection 23.2(1);
-- src:3938 | (j) subsection 23.3(1);
-- src:3939 | (k) subsection 28(7);
-- src:3940 | (l) paragraph 29(a);
-- src:3941 | (m) subsections 30(1) and (4) to (7);
-- src:3942 | (n) section 51; and
-- src:3943 | (o) Schedule I.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2021, c. 23, s. 332 (src:3928)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 332 the earlier text of the listed provisions continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` IF
        `Act RP 2021 c. 23 ss. 332 to 335 and 2022 c. 10 s. 411 the band of the day a benefit period begins` `the first day of the benefit period` EQUALS `ei7 begins before September 27, 2020`
    OR  `Act RP 2021 c. 23 ss. 332 to 335 and 2022 c. 10 s. 411 the band of the day a benefit period begins` `the first day of the benefit period` EQUALS `ei7 begins from September 27, 2020 to September 25, 2021`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2021, c. 23, s. 332 (src:3929-3943)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 332 the provisions whose earlier text continues to apply` IS
    IF `Act RP 2021 c. 23 s. 332 the earlier text of the listed provisions continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period`
    THEN LIST `ei7 s 6(1) the definitions major attachment claimant and minor attachment claimant`
            , `ei7 s 7(2)`
            , `ei7 s 7.1(1)`
            , `ei7 s 12(8)`
            , `ei7 s 21(1)`
            , `ei7 ss 22(1), (2) and (5)`
            , `ei7 ss 23(1), (1.3), (4), (4.1), (5) and (6)`
            , `ei7 s 23.1(2)`
            , `ei7 s 23.2(1)`
            , `ei7 s 23.3(1)`
            , `ei7 s 28(7)`
            , `ei7 s 29(a)`
            , `ei7 ss 30(1) and (4) to (7)`
            , `ei7 s 51`
            , `ei7 Schedule I`
    ELSE EMPTY

