§ `2022, c. 10, ss. 406 and 411`

-- s. 406: the earlier Act continues to apply to agreements or arrangements entered into under Part II that are in force on
-- the day on which the Division comes into force. The agreements are between the Commission and others; the person in
-- the seat holds no claim under them.
-- src:3978 | — 2022, c. 10, s. 406
-- src:3979 | Agreements or arrangements
-- src:3980 | 406 The Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the day on which this Division comes into force, continues to apply to agreements or arrangements entered into under Part II of that Act that are in force on that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2022, c. 10, s. 406 (src:3980)
GIVEN `the agreement or arrangement was entered into under Part II of the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in force on the day on which the Division comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2022 c. 10 s. 406 the earlier Act continues to apply to the agreement or arrangement` IF
        `the agreement or arrangement was entered into under Part II of the Employment Insurance Act`
    AND `it is in force on the day on which the Division comes into force`

-- s. 411: Schedule V as it read immediately before September 25, 2022 continues to apply to a claimant whose benefit
-- period begins before that day.
-- src:3982 | — 2022, c. 10, s. 411
-- src:3983 | Continued application — before September 25, 2022
-- src:3984 | 411 Schedule V to the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before September 25, 2022, continues to apply in respect of a claimant whose benefit period, as those terms are defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, begins before September 25, 2022.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2022, c. 10, s. 411 (src:3984)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2022 c. 10 s. 411 Schedule V as it read immediately before September 25, 2022 continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` IF
        `Act RP 2021 c. 23 ss. 332 to 335 and 2022 c. 10 s. 411 the band of the day a benefit period begins` `the first day of the benefit period` EQUALS `ei7 begins before September 27, 2020`
    OR  `Act RP 2021 c. 23 ss. 332 to 335 and 2022 c. 10 s. 411 the band of the day a benefit period begins` `the first day of the benefit period` EQUALS `ei7 begins from September 27, 2020 to September 25, 2021`
    OR  `Act RP 2021 c. 23 ss. 332 to 335 and 2022 c. 10 s. 411 the band of the day a benefit period begins` `the first day of the benefit period` EQUALS `ei7 begins from September 26, 2021 to September 24, 2022`

§ `2023, c. 26, s. 664 - the bodies defined`

-- Each definition is worked out from the facts it names. "General Division" is defined "except for the purposes of
-- subsections 665(2) and 667(2)": there the definition does not apply and the section says nothing, so NOTHING.
-- src:3986 | — 2023, c. 26, s. 664
-- src:3987 | Definitions
-- src:3988 | 664 The following definitions apply in this section and sections 665 to 678.
-- src:3989 | Appeal Division means the Appeal Division of the Tribunal. (division d’appel)
-- src:3990 | Board of Appeal means the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act. (Conseil d’appel)
-- src:3991 | Employment Insurance Section means the Employment Insurance Section of the General Division. (section de l’assurance-emploi)
-- src:3992 | General Division means, except for the purposes of subsections 665(2) and 667(2), the General Division referred to in section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it reads on the day on which this section comes into force. (division générale)
-- src:3993 | Tribunal means the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act. (Tribunal)
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 664 "Appeal Division" (src:3989)
GIVEN `it is the Appeal Division of the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 664 Appeal Division` IF
    `it is the Appeal Division of the Tribunal`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 664 "Board of Appeal" (src:3990)
GIVEN `it is the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 664 Board of Appeal` IF
    `it is the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 664 "Employment Insurance Section" (src:3991)
GIVEN `it is the Employment Insurance Section of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 664 Employment Insurance Section` IF
    `it is the Employment Insurance Section of the General Division`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 664 "General Division" (src:3992)
GIVEN `it is the General Division referred to in section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it reads on the day on which section 664 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word is used in subsection 665(2) or 667(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 664 General Division` IS
    IF `the word is used in subsection 665(2) or 667(2)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `it is the General Division referred to in section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it reads on the day on which section 664 comes into force`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 664 "Tribunal" (src:3993)
GIVEN `it is the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 664 Tribunal` IF
    `it is the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

§ `2023, c. 26, s. 676 - section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

-- (1) section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 does not apply to a decision in relation to the Employment
-- Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act as it read immediately
-- before the day Division 20 of that Act comes into force, nor to an application under that section 66 in relation to
-- the Employment Insurance Act that is ongoing immediately before the day section 634 comes into force.
-- (2) any matter relating to such a decision or application is dealt with under section 66 as it then read.
-- src:3995 | — 2023, c. 26, s. 676
-- src:3996 | Section 241 of Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1
-- src:3997 | 676 (1) Section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 does not apply in respect of a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 comes into force, or in respect of an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act that is ongoing immediately before the day on which section 634 comes into force.
-- src:3998 | Section 66 of Department of Employment and Social Development Act
-- src:3999 | (2) Any matter relating to a decision or an application referred to in subsection (1) is to be dealt with in accordance with section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 comes into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 676(1) (src:3997)
GIVEN `it is a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is ongoing immediately before the day on which section 634 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 676(1) section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 does not apply` IF
        `it is a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 comes into force`
    OR  (    `it is an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act`
         AND `the application is ongoing immediately before the day on which section 634 comes into force`)

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2023, c. 26, s. 676(2) (src:3999)
GIVEN `it is a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is ongoing immediately before the day on which section 634 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 676(2) the matter is dealt with in accordance with section 66 as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 comes into force` IF
    `Act RP 2023 c. 26 s. 676(1) section 241 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 does not apply` `it is a decision in relation to the Employment Insurance Act under section 66 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it read immediately before the day on which Division 20 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2021, No. 1 comes into force` `it is an application under that section 66 in relation to the Employment Insurance Act` `the application is ongoing immediately before the day on which section 634 comes into force`
